From the 1E DMG:

****************
As with other magic bags, this one appears to be a common cloth sack of
about 2' x 4' size. The bag of holding opens into a non-dimensional space,
and its inside is larger than its outside dimensions. Regardless of what is
put into this item, the bag of holding always weighs a fixed amount. This
weight, the bag's weight limit in contents, and its volume content are
dependent upon its quality as shown below:

WEIGHT:     WEIGHT LIMIT:    VOLUME LIMIT:
15lbs             250 lbs                   30 cubic feet
15lbs             500 lbs                   70  "        "
35lbs             1000lbs                  150 "       "
60lbs             1500lbs                  250 "       "

If overloaded, or sharp objects are placed within so as to pierce it, the
bag will rupture and be ruined, and the  contents will be lost forever in
the vortices of nilspace.
*****************

There is no reference to the bags doing the explosion bit in the actual
description of the bag itself, oddly enough. There is also no bad
interaction between staves (not wands) of cancellation and the BoH. You can
even safely nest bags inside bags (which would be nice if you had one of
the smallest and one of the largest, but the largest inside the smallest
and the weight vanishes) The only negative consequences occured if you
tried combining a BoH with a Portable Hole, thusly:

**************
If a bag of holding is place within a portable hole, a rift to the Astral
Plane is torn in space, and the bag and the hole are sucked into the void
and forever lost. If a portable hole is placed within a bag of holding, it
opens a gate to another plane, and the 'hole, bag' and any creatures within
a 10' radius are drawn to the plane, the portable hole and bag of holding
being destroyed in the process.
*************



